          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            (or family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            of objects) in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is called a
            %em separator
            or
            %em generator
            if
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+elements"} generalized elements
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            (or domain from
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dual
            notion is that of a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coseparator"} coseparator
          %h2#Terminology Caution on terminology
          %p
            The term ‘generator’ is slightly more ambiguous because of the use of ‘generators’ in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generators and relations
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#motive"}
            (q.v.).
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in \mathcal{C}
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is called a
              %strong separator
              or a
              %strong generator
              or a
              %strong separating object
              or a
              = succeed "," do
                %strong generating object
              %strong separate morphisms
              if:
            %ul
              %li
                for every pair of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+morphisms"} parallel morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g \colon X \to Y
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi e
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\circ e = g\circ e
                for every morphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi S
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\colon S \to X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = g
          %p
            Equivalently, we have that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a separator if, for every object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:S\rightarrow X
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jointly+epimorphic+family"} jointly epic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small"} locally small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a separator if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+functor"} hom functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(S,-) \colon \mathcal{C} \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful
          %p More generally:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family"} family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S} = (S_a)_{(a \in A)}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              %strong separating family
              or a
              %strong generating family
              if:
            %ul
              %li
                for every pair of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+morphisms"} parallel morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g \colon X \to Y
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi e
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ e = g \circ e
                for every
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi a
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \colon S_a \to X
                sourced in the family, then
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo =
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = g
          %p
            Assuming again that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            is a separating family if the family of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+functors"} hom functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(S_a,-) \colon \mathcal{C} \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            (for
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jointly+faithful+family+of+functors"} jointly faithful
          %p
            If the separating family is given by a functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \colon \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a separator if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} nerve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo →
                  %mi Psh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(G-,-) \colon \mathcal{C} \to Psh(\mathcal{A})
            is faithful
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#JoachimLambek"} Lambek (Section 2.)
          %p
            Since repetition is irrelevant in a separating family, we may also speak of a
            %em
              separating
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
            instead of a separating family.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong separating set
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/size+issues"} small
              separating class.
          %h3#fibered In fibered categories
          %p
            The notion of separating family can be generalized from categories to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+categories"} fibered categories
            in such a way that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+fibration"} family fibration
            of a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            has a separating family if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            has a small separating family.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A separating family in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+category"} fibered category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P:\mathbf{E}\to \mathbf{B}
              is an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\in \mathbf{E}
              such that for every parallel pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g:A\to B
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\neq g
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(f) = P(g)
              there exist arrows
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c: X\to S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:X\to A
              (constituting a span) such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              is
              = succeed "-cartesian," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mi h
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi g
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f h \neq g h
              \.
          %p
            See Definition B2.4.1 in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
          %h2#examples_and_applications Examples and applications
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited set
                is a separator; in particular, the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
                is a separator.
            %li
              %p
                More generally, in any
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+category"} well-pointed category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                is a separator. More generally still, in any represented
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            %li
              %p
                The standard example of a separator in the category of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
                over a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^I
                (for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                an
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                (which is
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^I
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective object
                in the category of
                = succeed "-modules," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                = succeed ")" do
                  %em Abelian Categories
                = succeed "." do
                  %em progenerator
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+equivalence"} Morita equivalence
            %li
              %p
                The existence of a small separating family is one of the conditions in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giraud%27s+theorem"} Giraud's theorem
                characterizing
                = succeed "es." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            %li
              %p
                The existence of a small (co)separating family is one of the conditions in one version of the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
            %li
              %p
                In
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Set
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{op}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                is a separator, thus every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functor"} continuous functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %mi Set
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:Set\to C
                into a locally small category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                has a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                by the special
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
            %li
              %p
                On the other hand, the opposite of the category of groups does not admit a separator, since there exists a continuous functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ML
                      %mo :
                      %mi Group
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ML: Group\to Set
                which does not have a left adjoint (see Example 3.1 on the page
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
          %h2#strengthened_separators Strengthened separators
          #motive.num_theorem
            %h6#motivating_theorem Motivating theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small
              and has all small
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S_a)_{(a\colon A)}
              is separating if and only if, for every
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in C
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ε
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi a
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi a
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon_X\colon \coprod_{a\colon A, f\colon S_a \to X} S_a \longrightarrow X
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
          %p
            This theorem explains a likely origin of the term “generator” or “generating family”. For example, in linear algebra, one says that a set of morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_a: S_a \to X
            spans or generates
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            if the induced map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oplus S_a \to X
            maps epimorphically onto
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            In particular if every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            in our category is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular
            (for example any
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            can be realised as a colimit in the following way
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi coeq
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi a
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mi S
